# Shell scripts must keep LF endings on every platform. Git for Windows defaults
# to core.autocrlf=true, which would rewrite these on checkout — and a CRLF in
# the shebang makes the script fail with "bad interpreter: /bin/sh^M" rather
# than anything that points at the cause.
*.sh text eol=lf

# JSON manifests are read by tooling, not shells, but there is no reason for
# them to differ per platform either.
*.json text eol=lf
*.md text eol=lf
